      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The paper covers questions of etiology, pathogenesis, clinical and radiographic appearance and diagnosis of spinal osteomyelitis. Principles of conservative and surgical treatment are outlined. It is noted that pain in the spine associated with elevated body temperature and alterations in blood count may be suggestive of setting up inflammation (with occasional destruction) in the vertebra and adjacent structures."},
